  "prompt": "For each month from January to June 2025 and each country (accounts.country_code), LedgerLoop's logo churn rate: the country's accounts that churned in the month divided by its accounts with MRR at the end of the month before. The base of a month is the accounts with MRR at the end of the month before: those with a row in mrr_monthly for the month before (mrr_monthly.month is the first day of a month). An account churned in a month when it has a churn event (event_type churn in subscription_events) dated in that month; count each account once. An account that starts or comes back during the month is not in that month's base. Return three columns, in this order: month_start (the first day of the month), country_code and churn_rate, as a share (0.02 for 2%), not rounded. Return one row for each month and country with a base; a country with no churn in a month shows 0. Any row order is fine.",
